<#
.SYNOPSIS

Create Machine Account (v2)

.DESCRIPTION

Submits a machine account creation request. New integrations should use this operation. This operation accepts the same request and runs the same creation process as [Submit Machine Account Creation Request](https://developer.sailpoint.com/docs/api/create-machine-account-request-v-2). That operation stays on the account-requests API for integrations that already call it. When version 1 cannot create the account because the subtype is not tied to a single source, the error directs the caller here. This method validates the input data, processes the machine account creation request, and returns an asynchronous result containing a tracking ID.  Compared with v1, this version: - Accepts a `sourceId` so you can choose the source to create the account on. `sourceId` is required while tiered subtype configuration is enabled, and the subtype must be in that source's effective set. When that flag is off, `sourceId` is ignored and the source is the subtype's own source. - Accepts `entitlements` (comment, start date, and remove date) while per-entitlement request details are enabled. `entitlementIds` is honored while that flag is off. A non-empty list of the other kind returns `400`. - Supports subtypes that are not tied to a single source while tiered subtype configuration is enabled. Version 1 rejects those subtypes.  There is no v2 status endpoint. Use the returned `accountRequestId` with [Get Machine Account Creation Request](https://developer.sailpoint.com/docs/api/get-create-machine-account-request-v-1) to track the request.  This API returns `403` when machine identity creation is not included in the tenant's plan. When machine account creation is not enabled for the tenant, this API returns `404`.  This API requires the `sp:scopes:default` scope. >**NOTE: You can only request a machine account on a subtype for which you have a create machine account entitlement provisioned. Otherwise, this API returns `403`.** 

